  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ain Dara The remains of a temple at Ain Dara provide interesting early indications of later temple plans, such as that of the temple of Jerusalem. The Ain Dara temple existed during the transition from Bronze to Iron Ages.</p>\r\n<p>Turkish military activity reportedly inflicted heavy damage to the archaeological site on 27 January 2018.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Ain Dara, located northwest of Aleppo, Syria, is noted for the remains of an Iron Age Syro-Hittite temple.",
